"2283",""
"2284",""
"2285",""
"2286",""
"2287","On the authority of ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿĀmir, who said: ʿĀmir ibn Rabīʿah and Sahl ibn Ḥunayf set out intending to bathe. They went looking for a secluded place. ʿĀmir (the text in the Musnad reads ""Sahl,"" and that is the correct reading) removed a woolen cloak he was wearing. I looked at him and struck him with the evil eye. He went down to the water to bathe. I heard a gurgling sound from him in the water. I came to him and called him three times, but he did not answer me. I went to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. He came walking, wading into the water—it is as if I am looking at the whiteness of his shins. He struck his chest with his hand and said: ""O Allah, remove from him its heat, its chill, and its suffering."" He stood up. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""When one of you sees from his brother, or from himself, or from his wealth something that amazes him, let him invoke blessing upon it (say: Bārak Allāh fīh), for the evil eye is real."""
