"2306",""
"2307","Ibn ʿUmar said: “O Nāfiʿ, blood has become agitated in me, so find me a cupper and make him gentle, if you can, and do not make him an old man or a young boy. For I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Cupping on an empty stomach is best; in it there is healing and blessing, and it increases the intellect and memory. So get cupped with the blessing of Allah on Thursday, and avoid cupping on Wednesday, Friday, Saturday, and Sunday as a precaution. And get cupped on Monday and Tuesday, for that is the day on which Allah cured Ayyūb of the affliction, and He struck him with the affliction on Wednesday. Indeed, neither leprosy nor vitiligo appears except on Wednesday or the night of Wednesday.’”"
